1
00:00:01,608 --> 00:00:03,700
It's done. It's done!

2
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,536
It struck! Lightning struck!

3
00:00:14,536 --> 00:00:16,452
Love.

4
00:00:28,168 --> 00:00:30,108
Morning.

5
00:00:38,432 --> 00:00:40,320
Morning.

6
00:00:43,104 --> 00:00:46,940
Morning, morning, morning.

7
00:00:46,940 --> 00:00:49,568
Morning, morning, morning.

8
00:00:49,568 --> 00:00:52,933
It has spots, so how about Spotty-suke?

9
00:00:56,548 --> 00:01:00,532
Oh, wait. It's a hyena, so...

10
00:01:00,532 --> 00:01:02,667
How about Zero Leftovers-suke?

11
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:11,392
- Good morning...
- What...

12
00:01:11,392 --> 00:01:12,552
What is it?

13
00:01:12,552 --> 00:01:14,367
Are you Starving Burglar-suke?

14
00:01:14,367 --> 00:01:16,367
No, it isn't. Please eat this.

15
00:01:16,367 --> 00:01:20,656
- What?
- Time for Operation Brain Activation.

16
00:01:20,656 --> 00:01:24,396
You have a mountain of things to think about.

17
00:01:24,396 --> 00:01:26,744
Don't you know? I don't like fish.

18
00:01:26,744 --> 00:01:28,816
So, any ideas for the backstory?

19
00:01:28,816 --> 00:01:30,396
Does it have a family?

20
00:01:30,396 --> 00:01:32,592
Where did it come from? The savanna?

21
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:36,467
Also, it's got this fluffy tutu-like thing.
Does it do ballet?

22
00:01:36,467 --> 00:01:40,260
That's still just a faint hint...
or more like, an elegant touch?

23
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:43,376
And most importantly, what's its name?
Hey, what's its name?

24
00:01:44,016 --> 00:01:47,060
I just want to call it by name!

25
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:50,664
Like, "I love you!"
or, "You're cute!" or something.

26
00:01:50,664 --> 00:01:55,408
But it's always just "it, it, it"... Wow!

27
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:59,328
Oh, my!

28
00:02:02,116 --> 00:02:04,688
This part. What's the inspiration for it?

29
00:02:04,688 --> 00:02:07,167
Inspiration? Well, uh...

30
00:02:07,167 --> 00:02:08,876
Why a hyena, anyway?

31
00:02:08,876 --> 00:02:11,812
- Like I said, it just popped into my head.
- And what's with the tutu here?

32
00:02:11,812 --> 00:02:15,008
- Just as I thought, from my story...
- Hey, we've talked about this,

33
00:02:15,008 --> 00:02:17,200
- like, 20 times already, right?
- Oh, my!

34
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:21,956
Its birth has my influence in it,
my essence in it...

35
00:02:21,956 --> 00:02:28,200
Ah... I just want to call it
by name, name, name...

36
00:02:29,392 --> 00:02:33,800
It's like my child.
I'll give it the best name.

37
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,452
And then...

38
00:02:35,452 --> 00:02:37,356
- A huge hit.
- A huge hit.

39
00:02:39,968 --> 00:02:43,392
I have to go now.
So, please eat that. I mean it.

40
00:02:43,392 --> 00:02:46,268
And the backstory and the name.
Backstory and name!

41
00:02:46,268 --> 00:02:49,604
Backstory! Name!

42
00:02:51,328 --> 00:02:53,133
You don't have to be so considerate.

43
00:02:53,133 --> 00:02:56,000
I'm taking up your time when you're busy.

44
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,060
I'd appreciate your opinion
from a calm, neutral standpoint.

45
00:02:59,060 --> 00:03:02,012
Oh, so this is about
the plushie you're making?

46
00:03:02,692 --> 00:03:07,333
Well, so the production cost
is one million yen?

47
00:03:07,333 --> 00:03:12,240
That's after squeezing the recent profits
of Seo Design for all they're worth.

48
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:16,028
And the distribution... What?

49
00:03:16,028 --> 00:03:17,128
In-store only?

50
00:03:17,128 --> 00:03:19,432
We'll do a homepage and social media,

51
00:03:19,432 --> 00:03:21,952
but I want people to only be able
to buy it at the store.

52
00:03:21,952 --> 00:03:24,544
Like, I want them to touch it
before buying it.

53
00:03:24,544 --> 00:03:28,816
That retro approach might
actually spark some interest.

54
00:03:28,816 --> 00:03:29,936
I see.

55
00:03:29,936 --> 00:03:33,912
So right now I'm struggling with
how to use that one million yen.

56
00:03:33,912 --> 00:03:36,908
I want to make the most of a limited budget.

57
00:03:36,908 --> 00:03:38,380
One million yen, huh?

58
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:43,024
So, I'm really sorry, but if any ideas
come to mind, could you hit me up?

59
00:03:43,024 --> 00:03:44,512
Sorry, I have to go now.

60
00:03:44,512 --> 00:03:47,348
- What?
- I want to go check out a few toy stores.

61
00:03:47,348 --> 00:03:49,212
The plushie isn't finished yet, right?

62
00:03:49,212 --> 00:03:51,264
No, but I want to be ready to
display it as soon as it's done.

63
00:03:51,264 --> 00:03:54,372
Ah, well then... Just to confirm.

64
00:03:54,372 --> 00:03:56,856
- About your fee...
- Oh, yeah! Guess what?

65
00:03:56,856 --> 00:03:59,096
The plushie sample arrives tomorrow!

66
00:03:59,096 --> 00:04:01,510
Oh, my! It's just an 'Oh, my' kind of day!

67
00:04:01,510 --> 00:04:03,012
Well then, take your time!

68
00:04:03,012 --> 00:04:06,228
- Huh? No... Wait...
- Thanks!

69
00:04:11,828 --> 00:04:14,952
[Mugi]

70
00:04:14,952 --> 00:04:16,876
Sorry!

71
00:04:22,248 --> 00:04:25,472
What? Could it be that
you're also thinking about a name?

72
00:04:25,472 --> 00:04:27,376
- A name?
- Yeah.

73
00:04:27,376 --> 00:04:31,228
No, an acquaintance of mine
treated me to a fancy meal,

74
00:04:31,228 --> 00:04:33,952
as a sort of consultation fee.

75
00:04:33,952 --> 00:04:35,392
But according to my info,

76
00:04:35,392 --> 00:04:39,380
the company that person is at
has been defaulting on payments,

77
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:42,680
and that meal was probably
paid for out of pocket.

78
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:45,820
Wow, a fancy meal. Nice.

79
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:48,192
All I got was fish! Fish!

80
00:04:48,192 --> 00:04:51,836
Well, I feel like that person
is being exploited for passion.

81
00:04:51,836 --> 00:04:54,233
Exploited for passion...

82
00:04:54,233 --> 00:04:56,500
Well... What exactly is that again?

83
00:04:56,500 --> 00:05:00,480
It's when someone uses your passion
or experience as an excuse

84
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:04,132
to make you work for cheap or for free.

85
00:05:04,952 --> 00:05:07,280
I feel like someone was doing that to me...

86
00:05:08,952 --> 00:05:11,572
<i>Takai Create.</i>

87
00:05:11,572 --> 00:05:12,700
Ah, no.

88
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:14,780
I feel like someone else was doing it too...

89
00:05:14,780 --> 00:05:16,902
These days, exploiting passion

90
00:05:16,902 --> 00:05:20,172
- is an immediate red flag.
- Who was it again?

91
00:05:20,172 --> 00:05:23,300
Just the other day,
a company promised verbally

92
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:27,008
to pay based on results,
but kept stiffing people.

93
00:05:27,008 --> 00:05:31,960
That company got massively flamed
for passion exploitation,

94
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:34,832
and then ended up going bankrupt. Bankrupt.

95
00:05:34,832 --> 00:05:36,804
Based on results...

96
00:05:36,804 --> 00:05:39,008
You can pay me based on the results.

97
00:05:40,028 --> 00:05:41,440
- That's me!
- Well,

98
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:43,916
if that kind of
shady management continues,

99
00:05:43,916 --> 00:05:47,380
I do think my acquaintance
will eventually quit.

100
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:48,976
What about deferred payment
based on future success?

101
00:05:48,976 --> 00:05:50,692
Is paying later based on future success
also bad? The same thing?

102
00:05:50,692 --> 00:05:54,440
If you're attaching uncertain conditions
to the payment of a fee,

103
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,500
it's the same thing.

104
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:57,244
The same thing?

105
00:05:57,244 --> 00:05:59,840
Takai Create and me?

106
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:02,400
I'm Takai, from Takai Create.

107
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,956
Famous for the name Takai,
but also for fees that are low.

108
00:06:04,956 --> 00:06:08,620
Thank you very much for agreeing with
our company's business philosophy.

109
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:10,708
Thank you very much.

110
00:06:10,708 --> 00:06:12,490
No, no, no! I'm not agreeing!

111
00:06:12,490 --> 00:06:14,424
Non-payment, cheap rates, very welcome!

112
00:06:14,424 --> 00:06:16,200
If we're found out, bring on bankruptcy!

113
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:20,396
Now, let's advance together,
into the garden of passion exploitation!

114
00:06:20,396 --> 00:06:23,576
I said, I'm not into passion exploitation!

115
00:06:23,576 --> 00:06:26,573
Well... Are you okay?

116
00:06:43,692 --> 00:06:45,976
Oh, my, it's no use! I can't focus.

117
00:06:45,976 --> 00:06:47,760
Thinking about the plushie sample arriving,

118
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:49,948
I'm just so wired
that being subtle is impossible.

119
00:06:49,948 --> 00:06:52,167
Look, my hands are sweating like crazy...

120
00:06:53,132 --> 00:06:55,100
What are you...

121
00:06:56,536 --> 00:06:59,284
Here's 500,000 yen for your consulting fee.

122
00:07:00,172 --> 00:07:02,392
Where did this come from?

123
00:07:02,392 --> 00:07:04,656
Well... an investment, I guess?

124
00:07:04,656 --> 00:07:06,300
There's a good one right now.

125
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:09,032
Like a new big bro? Something like that.

126
00:07:09,032 --> 00:07:13,212
- Sort of a new older brother?
- Where did this come from?

127
00:07:14,104 --> 00:07:17,608
From the one million yen
for the plushie production.

128
00:07:17,608 --> 00:07:20,652
So are you telling me to make it
with the remaining 500,000?

129
00:07:20,652 --> 00:07:22,944
The plushie of this?

130
00:07:22,944 --> 00:07:25,276
Well, yes, that's what it means.

131
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:27,292
Thank you for the sentiment.

132
00:07:27,292 --> 00:07:29,850
But as I said before,
the consulting fee could be paid

133
00:07:29,850 --> 00:07:31,600
- based on results...
- I said no!

134
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,928
That would make me the same!

135
00:07:32,928 --> 00:07:35,076
What... What are you...

136
00:07:35,076 --> 00:07:39,156
Besides, even one million was really tight,
so 500,000 is way too little!

137
00:07:39,156 --> 00:07:40,884
For its sake, we absolutely
need that one million yen...

138
00:07:40,884 --> 00:07:42,984
This is also for its sake!

139
00:07:42,984 --> 00:07:46,460
In fact, not accepting this
would be worse for it!

140
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:49,784
What? How is any of that for its...

141
00:07:50,988 --> 00:07:54,472
It's here! Oh, my!

142
00:07:55,672 --> 00:07:58,180
Anyway, let's put that conversation on hold.

143
00:07:59,648 --> 00:08:01,464
Time to take a look.

144
00:08:08,124 --> 00:08:11,100
Welcome to our home!

145
00:08:15,533 --> 00:08:17,696
Who's this?

146
00:08:17,696 --> 00:08:20,700
Ah!

147
00:08:28,428 --> 00:08:30,552
[Episode 4]
I told you clearly, didn't I?

148
00:08:30,552 --> 00:08:33,772
That it's a hyena with
a fluffy tutu-like thing.

149
00:08:33,772 --> 00:08:36,036
And this is a rice cake?

150
00:08:36,036 --> 00:08:38,240
You changed it to
a freshly pounded rice cake?

151
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,948
What about the factory?

152
00:08:40,740 --> 00:08:42,928
Which country did you say?

153
00:08:42,928 --> 00:08:45,148
The Republic of Textorian?

154
00:08:45,148 --> 00:08:48,584
Anyway, just please check with the site.

155
00:08:48,584 --> 00:08:50,467
Please.

156
00:08:50,467 --> 00:08:52,304
- Wow!
- Wow!

157
00:08:52,304 --> 00:08:55,908
- Sorry for interrupting your call.
- No problem.

158
00:08:55,908 --> 00:08:57,836
What? Are you going on a business trip?

159
00:08:57,836 --> 00:09:01,856
A business trip?
Oh, right, I didn't tell you.

160
00:09:01,856 --> 00:09:04,600
I quit Merry.

161
00:09:05,332 --> 00:09:08,376
- Mandatory retirement...
- No, not that.

162
00:09:08,376 --> 00:09:11,216
Well... I had various things to think about.

163
00:09:13,676 --> 00:09:15,988
Huh? What's this?

164
00:09:15,988 --> 00:09:18,348
I know! A freshly pounded rice cake, right?

165
00:09:18,348 --> 00:09:21,348
No, it's a sample of a new character.

166
00:09:21,348 --> 00:09:25,024
And this is the real one.

167
00:09:27,892 --> 00:09:29,736
Cute!

168
00:09:29,736 --> 00:09:34,496
What? Could this be a hyena?
It's insanely cute!

169
00:09:34,496 --> 00:09:39,408
Just as I'd expect from you, Mr. Hirose.
It's just so... so...

170
00:09:39,408 --> 00:09:42,552
- Oh, my!
- Oh, my!

171
00:09:43,848 --> 00:09:47,816
But for some reason, it turned into
that freshly pounded rice cake thing.

172
00:09:47,816 --> 00:09:50,272
By the way, did Mr. Seo make the pattern?

173
00:09:50,272 --> 00:09:51,392
[Pattern: Paper guide for plushie-making,]
No, the factory said

174
00:09:51,392 --> 00:09:53,524
[cutting, and sewing into 3D dolls]
they were good at patterns, so...

175
00:09:53,524 --> 00:09:56,820
If I'd known it was going to turn out like
a rice cake, I would have made it myself!

176
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:59,492
I'll make the pattern.

177
00:09:59,492 --> 00:10:03,460
- What?
- No, I mean, because it's so cute...

178
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:06,620
No, I mean, I want to make it!
I want to make it like crazy!

179
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:08,704
Please! I'm begging you!

180
00:10:08,704 --> 00:10:12,256
Let me go crazy with its pattern!

181
00:10:12,256 --> 00:10:14,080
And of course, I don't need any money!

182
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:17,508
- No, wait! That's totally not allowed.
- No, it's absolutely not allowed.

183
00:10:17,508 --> 00:10:19,404
So...

184
00:10:23,608 --> 00:10:25,580
This isn't much, but...

185
00:10:30,056 --> 00:10:33,056
Let me show you work
that's worth 100 times this!

186
00:10:38,464 --> 00:10:41,888
Starting from Germany,
the home of the original teddy bear,

187
00:10:41,888 --> 00:10:47,564
Europe, Asia, the Middle East, Africa...

188
00:10:47,564 --> 00:10:50,384
Seeing plushies from all over the world

189
00:10:50,384 --> 00:10:54,360
became a journey to rediscover what I love.

190
00:10:55,100 --> 00:10:58,933
To the two who gave me this chance,
I'm truly grateful.

191
00:10:58,933 --> 00:11:03,367
No, we didn't do anything.
No gratitude necessary.

192
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:09,728
I wanted to return that feeling of gratitude,

193
00:11:09,728 --> 00:11:12,252
so I was looking for souvenirs.

194
00:11:12,252 --> 00:11:14,300
I found this at a secondhand store
in the Czech Republic.

195
00:11:14,300 --> 00:11:18,684
Even though it's from decades ago,
it's in good condition.

196
00:11:22,324 --> 00:11:29,108
I thought, "Berry was loved by someone
even in a faraway country."

197
00:11:29,108 --> 00:11:32,084
I want to do that kind of work again.

198
00:11:35,208 --> 00:11:39,867
So I'm really happy
that we can work together again.

199
00:11:49,324 --> 00:11:50,840
Well...

200
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:53,984
Thank... Thank you.

201
00:11:53,984 --> 00:11:55,780
No gratitude necessary.

202
00:12:03,108 --> 00:12:04,424
No way!

203
00:12:04,424 --> 00:12:08,248
You have zero interest in cute things,
Ms. Kusakabe, so here, take this!

204
00:12:08,248 --> 00:12:12,216
Peanuts! So many...

205
00:12:14,396 --> 00:12:18,184
Well, do you properly understand
the meaning of a harsh review?

206
00:12:18,184 --> 00:12:20,924
- Yes.
- Please forget it quickly.

207
00:12:20,924 --> 00:12:22,512
The old Merry style.

208
00:12:22,512 --> 00:12:25,360
Understood. I'll correct it.

209
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:27,633
The coordination with major
goods shops is also done.

210
00:12:27,633 --> 00:12:28,804
We can secure a very good spot

211
00:12:28,804 --> 00:12:31,504
for the first week of
Harsh Review Molco's launch.

212
00:12:31,504 --> 00:12:32,616
I see.

213
00:12:32,616 --> 00:12:35,733
The launch date is also as you instructed.

214
00:12:36,608 --> 00:12:38,512
Mr. Omishima.

215
00:12:39,348 --> 00:12:42,972
There's a rumor that Director Yamakawa
of Product Planning is resigning.

216
00:12:44,564 --> 00:12:47,668
He says that if Mr. Hirose quits,
then so will he.

217
00:12:49,708 --> 00:12:51,892
That's convenient.

218
00:12:51,892 --> 00:12:57,100
Low-level talent like that
will eventually drag the company down.

219
00:13:05,492 --> 00:13:09,432
I see! To show your love for that character,

220
00:13:09,432 --> 00:13:13,512
that "Oh, my" from earlier
was kind of like "Oh, my," right?

221
00:13:13,512 --> 00:13:18,464
But it feels like I'm holding back somehow.

222
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:19,804
I understand.

223
00:13:19,804 --> 00:13:24,532
But I think you should be
more honest about what you love.

224
00:13:25,552 --> 00:13:31,804
I myself think I would have regretted it
if I had stayed at Merry.

225
00:13:31,804 --> 00:13:36,908
So don't hold back.
Go full throttle and enjoy your love.

226
00:13:36,908 --> 00:13:39,467
A rising dragon... Ouch!

227
00:13:40,188 --> 00:13:41,996
Full...

228
00:13:43,564 --> 00:13:45,476
throttle.

229
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:51,176
<i>♪ I can live without love ♪</i>

230
00:13:51,176 --> 00:13:56,266
<i>♪ Goodbye to the past where I believed that ♪</i>

231
00:13:56,266 --> 00:14:01,076
<i>♪ I can't live without love ♪</i>

232
00:14:01,076 --> 00:14:06,156
<i>♪ Out of my way, heart-pounding full speed ♪</i>

233
00:14:06,156 --> 00:14:11,584
<i>♪ Now, all at once ♪</i>

234
00:14:11,584 --> 00:14:20,648
<i>♪ I love it all ♪</i>

235
00:14:20,648 --> 00:14:26,800
[Mugi]
<i>♪ I love it for no particular reason ♪</i>

236
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:28,704
Any response?

237
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:35,488
[Anna]

238
00:14:35,488 --> 00:14:36,676
[Production Cost]
If I pay 400,000,

239
00:14:36,676 --> 00:14:40,067
[Kusakabe, Hirose]
it's not passion exploitation.

240
00:14:40,756 --> 00:14:43,936
Mr. Seo, I'm going full throttle.
No holding back.

241
00:14:43,936 --> 00:14:45,468
What?

242
00:14:45,468 --> 00:14:47,567
To get our character
to as many people as possible,

243
00:14:47,567 --> 00:14:50,296
I'm going full throttle, no holding back.

244
00:14:50,296 --> 00:14:51,608
Oh...

245
00:14:51,608 --> 00:14:54,756
So first, I'll establish
a research institute for it.

246
00:14:54,756 --> 00:14:57,774
A brain trust that gathers experts
to research cuteness.

247
00:14:57,774 --> 00:15:01,032
I'll name it... the Cute Think Tank.

248
00:15:01,032 --> 00:15:02,467
Cute Gun Tank?

249
00:15:02,467 --> 00:15:04,684
We'll research its cuteness
and reason for being.

250
00:15:04,684 --> 00:15:05,922
[Think tank: Experts researching]
Academically research,

251
00:15:05,922 --> 00:15:07,156
[business issues to guide strategy]
investigate, and analyze,

252
00:15:07,156 --> 00:15:10,724
and add value so that everyone
who sees it wants to hold it.

253
00:15:10,724 --> 00:15:13,400
We'll add that kind of added value.

254
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:16,724
- Added value...
- Now, let me introduce the members.

255
00:15:16,724 --> 00:15:18,424
Please.

256
00:15:18,424 --> 00:15:20,284
Nice to meet you.

257
00:15:20,284 --> 00:15:22,860
I'm Tomioka Accele.

258
00:15:24,876 --> 00:15:26,260
Huh? Wait... What... What?

259
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:28,280
Mr. Accele worked in the planning
and strategy department

260
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:29,344
of a major advertising agency.

261
00:15:29,344 --> 00:15:32,584
He went independent three years ago,
and is now active worldwide

262
00:15:32,584 --> 00:15:35,400
[Tomioka Accele]
as a brand strategist.

263
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:36,780
Stra... Strategist?

264
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:41,860
Mr. Seo, humans are always seeking
their own special something.

265
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:47,680
So I advocate for a secretly special feeling.

266
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:49,084
Secret...

267
00:15:49,084 --> 00:15:51,764
What is this? What is this person saying?

268
00:15:51,764 --> 00:15:55,420
For example, for this character's
eye material,

269
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:57,040
we could secretly change it

270
00:15:57,040 --> 00:16:00,320
to a lacquered one
handled by a Wajima craftsman.

271
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:05,452
This secretly special feeling
secretly stimulates the desire to own...

272
00:16:05,452 --> 00:16:07,388
This is Ms. Sachie Sachi.

273
00:16:07,388 --> 00:16:10,932
Are you happy? I'm happy.

274
00:16:10,932 --> 00:16:13,608
[Sachie Sachi]
I'm Sachie Sachi.

275
00:16:13,608 --> 00:16:15,632
Huh? This person too?

276
00:16:15,632 --> 00:16:17,576
A member of the Cute Think Tank.

277
00:16:17,576 --> 00:16:20,416
Ms. Sachie earned a doctorate
in psychology in Brazil,

278
00:16:20,416 --> 00:16:24,168
and is now active in the media
as an IP Happy strategist.

279
00:16:24,168 --> 00:16:26,768
I've heard that your company's 'Happy'

280
00:16:26,768 --> 00:16:30,216
is to deliver this plushie to more people.

281
00:16:30,216 --> 00:16:35,692
So, I recommend giving
this character a 'Happy' item.

282
00:16:35,692 --> 00:16:39,280
IP refers to intellectual property
like characters and works.

283
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:43,900
Hello Kitty, Snoopy,
Anpanman, they're all IP.

284
00:16:43,900 --> 00:16:49,564
This strategy of adding
such a 'Happy' item on top...

285
00:16:49,564 --> 00:16:51,940
- Are you happy?
- Are you happy?

286
00:16:51,940 --> 00:16:53,980
- No.
- So, the recommended

287
00:16:53,980 --> 00:16:57,668
'Happy' item this time
is a golden lotus root.

288
00:16:57,668 --> 00:16:59,767
Hello, my name is Shinako.

289
00:17:00,556 --> 00:17:02,640
Ms. Shinako is a Harajuku-style creator

290
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,208
[Influencer Shinako]
with a deep knowledge of cuteness.

291
00:17:04,208 --> 00:17:07,328
She is an influencer with lots of support
from the younger generation.

292
00:17:07,328 --> 00:17:11,980
Today, I'd like to eat this character.

293
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:14,960
- Eat?
- I'm going to dig in now.

294
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:16,860
What... What are you making
without permission?

295
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:19,452
- Hey.
- Shh... Listen.

296
00:17:19,452 --> 00:17:21,400
First, listen.

297
00:17:27,028 --> 00:17:29,600
- Right?
- Right?

298
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:32,364
Adding a gimmick
that makes a nice sound when bitten.

299
00:17:32,364 --> 00:17:34,056
It's worth doing.

300
00:17:37,296 --> 00:17:39,356
Secretly... IP...

301
00:17:39,356 --> 00:17:41,628
- Item... Gimmick...
- We could discuss the materials and such,

302
00:17:41,628 --> 00:17:43,296
but I think it's worth doing.

303
00:17:43,296 --> 00:17:46,992
- Since that's the case, then...
- What?

304
00:17:46,992 --> 00:17:49,108
500,000 yen for the plushie production
is far too little.

305
00:17:49,108 --> 00:17:52,172
Let's go with the remaining 900,000,
all of it. Let's pour it in.

306
00:17:52,172 --> 00:17:55,467
- That's why I said...
- Please don't worry about my fee.

307
00:17:55,467 --> 00:17:58,168
- I will worry, because of that...
- It's all for this character.

308
00:17:58,168 --> 00:17:59,980
It's for the character's sake,
on my side too!

309
00:17:59,980 --> 00:18:02,112
Full throttle, no holding back.
Come on, Mr. Seo, you too.

310
00:18:02,112 --> 00:18:04,104
- I won't do it.
- Full throttle, no holding back.

311
00:18:04,104 --> 00:18:08,572
Full throttle, no holding back...

312
00:18:08,572 --> 00:18:11,604
Full throttle, no holding back, full...

313
00:18:11,604 --> 00:18:14,800
At this rate, the entire amount
will go to production costs.

314
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:19,200
That'll be passion exploitation
and malnutrition confirmed.

315
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:21,400
Flaming, bankruptcy...

316
00:18:24,972 --> 00:18:27,528
There's no way I'll let that happen.

317
00:18:31,452 --> 00:18:33,212
A hallucination again?

318
00:18:36,408 --> 00:18:38,860
And it's coming closer!

319
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:42,228
A hallucination!
Another hallucination is coming!

320
00:18:42,228 --> 00:18:43,760
It's been a while, Mr. Seo.

321
00:18:43,760 --> 00:18:45,744
The hallucination called my name!

322
00:18:47,364 --> 00:18:49,800
What?

323
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:57,067
I am very sorry.

324
00:19:00,492 --> 00:19:02,336
I understand.

325
00:19:02,336 --> 00:19:05,876
I understand why you'd look at me that way.

326
00:19:05,876 --> 00:19:08,733
Since that day, I've turned over a new leaf.

327
00:19:09,504 --> 00:19:14,956
To live up to the name Takai,
I'm paying high compensation.

328
00:19:14,956 --> 00:19:17,033
And, well...

329
00:19:18,292 --> 00:19:24,167
Today I wanted to ask you
to do a job for me, Mr. Seo.

330
00:19:26,208 --> 00:19:28,260
[Production Request Form]
This is... the picture I drew.

331
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:35,176
Could you draw other characters
in the same style as this one?

332
00:19:35,176 --> 00:19:37,008
It's an important time for us right now.

333
00:19:37,008 --> 00:19:39,348
I don't want to cause any trouble.

334
00:19:39,348 --> 00:19:43,372
And frankly, your face looks suspicious.

335
00:19:44,428 --> 00:19:47,132
So I'm offering 100,000 yen per character.

336
00:19:47,132 --> 00:19:49,316
And ten of them.

337
00:19:49,316 --> 00:19:51,744
Ten... That means...

338
00:19:51,744 --> 00:19:54,900
- That means...
- One million yen.

339
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:01,724
I see. Got it. Well, I look forward
to working with you.

340
00:20:01,724 --> 00:20:03,712
Yes. All right, please excuse me.

341
00:20:03,712 --> 00:20:06,040
Hey, wait... Anna! Anna!

342
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:08,688
Ah, Mugi! Sorry, I didn't notice you.

343
00:20:08,688 --> 00:20:10,304
Working late is tough, huh?

344
00:20:10,304 --> 00:20:12,544
I'm sorry about that phone call earlier.

345
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:16,016
I meant to call you back, I meant to,
but when I got home...

346
00:20:16,016 --> 00:20:17,696
It's okay. Don't worry about it.

347
00:20:17,696 --> 00:20:19,416
Well, you're coming, right?
Let's go. Let's go.

348
00:20:19,416 --> 00:20:22,264
Ah, well... Today, I... Well...

349
00:20:22,264 --> 00:20:24,767
I was hoping we could talk here.

350
00:20:26,620 --> 00:20:28,324
Is that so?

351
00:20:29,392 --> 00:20:32,933
Well... Anna.

352
00:20:34,004 --> 00:20:35,788
Let's break up.

353
00:20:37,680 --> 00:20:40,524
Or rather, I want you to break up with me.

354
00:20:41,228 --> 00:20:45,056
- Wait, wait... What do you...
- I've met someone I like.

355
00:20:46,264 --> 00:20:50,656
You've met someone you like...

356
00:20:50,656 --> 00:20:52,720
Sorry, sorry.

357
00:20:57,308 --> 00:20:59,104
Hello.

358
00:21:01,148 --> 00:21:03,040
So, this is the situation.

359
00:21:04,892 --> 00:21:06,900
Sorry.

360
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:08,920
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

361
00:21:16,940 --> 00:21:19,633
And then... And then...

362
00:21:19,633 --> 00:21:23,867
And then... And then...

363
00:21:49,380 --> 00:21:55,544
[Official Character Launch Event]
<i>♪ I'll always think of you, muscles ♪</i>

364
00:21:55,544 --> 00:21:59,970
- <i>♪ Love, this is love, this is love ♪</i>
- Come on! Come on! Come on!

365
00:21:59,970 --> 00:22:03,364
- <i>♪ Love, love, love... ♪</i>
- Come on! Come on! Come on!

366
00:22:03,364 --> 00:22:05,767
Zapaan.

367
00:22:06,628 --> 00:22:09,400
Hey, you look pale.

368
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,548
Are you eating properly?

369
00:22:11,548 --> 00:22:14,828
Nothing seems to go down my throat.

370
00:22:15,520 --> 00:22:17,380
Nice muscles!

371
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:19,346
Everyone!

372
00:22:20,088 --> 00:22:22,699
- Thank you!
- Mugi...

373
00:22:22,699 --> 00:22:23,848
Why?

374
00:22:23,848 --> 00:22:27,633
Next up is the long-awaited
Muscle Shoulder Ride event!

375
00:22:28,656 --> 00:22:30,570
Zapaan, which comes with a chance
to win a shoulder ride ticket,

376
00:22:30,570 --> 00:22:33,044
is on sale over there.

377
00:22:33,044 --> 00:22:35,244
See you later.

378
00:22:36,072 --> 00:22:38,196
Mugi...

379
00:22:39,348 --> 00:22:42,736
100 Zapaans, please.

380
00:22:42,736 --> 00:22:45,032
Yeah! Thank you very much!

381
00:22:45,032 --> 00:22:46,836
Right this way!

382
00:22:46,836 --> 00:22:49,284
This customer is receiving 100 bottles.

383
00:22:49,284 --> 00:22:51,120
Thank you very much.

384
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,268
- Hurry, hurry!
- Yes.

385
00:22:53,268 --> 00:22:55,020
Why is she in a place like this?

386
00:22:55,020 --> 00:22:58,368
Why? Because she's a fan, obviously!

387
00:22:58,368 --> 00:23:01,536
[Not a winner]
A fan? Of the muscular guy? Mariko Mondo?

388
00:23:01,536 --> 00:23:02,852
What? Is she an acquaintance of yours?

389
00:23:02,852 --> 00:23:04,672
No, no. Wait, you don't know?

390
00:23:04,672 --> 00:23:06,700
She's the designer of Berry!

391
00:23:06,700 --> 00:23:09,196
What? Really? Seriously?

392
00:23:09,196 --> 00:23:12,133
- I'm even wearing Berry socks today!
- I'm not... I'm not interested.

393
00:23:12,133 --> 00:23:15,288
- Here, look...
- What's going on?

394
00:23:15,288 --> 00:23:17,016
Sorry, it's nothing.

395
00:23:17,016 --> 00:23:20,412
Sorry, this girl is a bit
emotionally unstable.

396
00:23:20,412 --> 00:23:23,028
Apparently she got dumped
by her boyfriend yesterday.

397
00:23:23,028 --> 00:23:25,976
Hey, don't just go
casually telling people that!

398
00:23:25,976 --> 00:23:27,772
Sorry.

399
00:23:27,772 --> 00:23:29,928
Fancied anyone?

400
00:23:29,928 --> 00:23:33,280
Some young girl...

401
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:35,460
I'm not talking about your boyfriend.

402
00:23:35,460 --> 00:23:37,572
I meant you.

403
00:23:37,572 --> 00:23:38,624
What?

404
00:23:38,624 --> 00:23:42,996
If that's the case,
it's only natural that you'd be dumped.

405
00:23:42,996 --> 00:23:47,520
The things you fancy are tremendously big.

406
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:52,733
If you keep holding them,
something will inevitably spill out.

407
00:23:54,324 --> 00:24:01,100
Didn't you have that kind of resolve?

408
00:24:02,088 --> 00:24:06,467
Here it is! Muscle Shoulder Ride!

409
00:24:10,816 --> 00:24:13,948
[Character Submission Materials]
This is great.

410
00:24:13,948 --> 00:24:16,067
It's all great.

411
00:24:16,067 --> 00:24:19,108
- A wave is coming.
- A wave.

412
00:24:19,108 --> 00:24:24,076
The promised one million yen.
I'll transfer it to you tomorrow.

413
00:24:26,748 --> 00:24:29,467
With this, the consulting fee...

414
00:24:38,040 --> 00:24:41,260
<i>Well, about that schedule,
is everyone okay with it?</i>

415
00:24:41,260 --> 00:24:42,432
- <i>Sachie is okay with it!</i>
- <i>Yes.</i>

416
00:24:42,432 --> 00:24:44,608
- <i>Yes! Shinako is okay with it!</i>
- <i>It's okay.</i>

417
00:24:44,608 --> 00:24:46,556
<i>Accele is also okay with it.</i>

418
00:24:47,434 --> 00:24:50,967
All right, let's call it a day.
Thank you all for your hard work.

419
00:24:50,967 --> 00:24:52,424
<i>Thank you for your hard work.</i>

420
00:24:52,424 --> 00:24:53,967
- <i>Thank you for your hard work.</i>
- <i>Thanks for your hard work.</i>

421
00:24:53,967 --> 00:24:56,792
What? There was a Gun Tank today?

422
00:24:56,792 --> 00:24:58,300
You should have woken me up.

423
00:24:58,300 --> 00:25:00,836
Sorry, but you didn't look like
you were very awake.

424
00:25:00,836 --> 00:25:04,244
Besides, it can't start without me.

425
00:25:04,244 --> 00:25:06,756
I'm a one-million-yen man, you know?

426
00:25:06,756 --> 00:25:09,700
Haven't you heard? Million-Yen Mizuki Seo.

427
00:25:09,700 --> 00:25:12,416
Or Trending Wave Mizuki Seo.

428
00:25:12,416 --> 00:25:16,028
- Or Seo's Wave is natural...
- Well, it's a bit early,

429
00:25:16,028 --> 00:25:17,468
but I'll be going home now.

430
00:25:17,468 --> 00:25:19,316
Thank you for your hard work.

431
00:25:27,052 --> 00:25:29,667
Something's weird, isn't it?

432
00:25:30,560 --> 00:25:33,316
Oh, the bread is bigger than usual.

433
00:25:33,316 --> 00:25:35,064
That's rich.

434
00:25:35,064 --> 00:25:38,416
No, not rich. It's the wave, you know.

435
00:25:38,416 --> 00:25:39,984
The wave is really coming.

436
00:25:39,984 --> 00:25:45,810
We're in a different phase from companies
that exploit passion, so to speak.

437
00:25:45,810 --> 00:25:47,516
Big wave.

438
00:25:47,516 --> 00:25:49,180
- Wave.
- That's nice.

439
00:25:49,180 --> 00:25:51,067
Compared to that, I'm...

440
00:25:51,067 --> 00:25:54,433
What? I'll listen to your troubles.

441
00:25:55,776 --> 00:25:59,896
I tend to ride the wave
and listen to troubles.

442
00:25:59,896 --> 00:26:03,248
No, actually, recently,

443
00:26:03,248 --> 00:26:06,980
I introduced some people knowledgeable
in a certain genre to an acquaintance,

444
00:26:06,980 --> 00:26:11,267
but then later I realized they charge
a pretty hefty consultation fee.

445
00:26:11,267 --> 00:26:14,292
What? So they charge money
just for giving advice?

446
00:26:14,292 --> 00:26:16,233
Seriously, who is that dude
with such a sweet gig?

447
00:26:16,233 --> 00:26:19,764
Do you know a guy named Tomioka Accele?

448
00:26:20,400 --> 00:26:22,576
Tomioka Accele.

449
00:26:24,292 --> 00:26:28,244
Seems like his fees start at
300,000 yen per session.

450
00:26:28,244 --> 00:26:32,716
My acquaintance is probably
paying that money out of pocket.

451
00:26:37,736 --> 00:26:39,496
Good morning.

452
00:26:42,084 --> 00:26:45,116
- Well...
- My grandma used to say that

453
00:26:45,116 --> 00:26:49,567
people who are hiding something
usually greet you with a loud voice.

454
00:26:50,572 --> 00:26:52,260
What are you talking about?

455
00:26:52,260 --> 00:26:56,552
Once upon a time, at a certain design office,

456
00:26:56,552 --> 00:26:59,636
there was a consultant named O-Con.

457
00:27:00,536 --> 00:27:03,018
One day, O-Con gathered his companions,

458
00:27:03,018 --> 00:27:06,776
whose names were Accele, Happy, and Shina,

459
00:27:06,776 --> 00:27:08,433
and established Gun Tank Consulting.

460
00:27:08,433 --> 00:27:12,492
- What are you talking about?
- However, those companions

461
00:27:13,560 --> 00:27:16,760
all charged outrageous consultation fees.

462
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:19,400
The office didn't have that kind of money.

463
00:27:19,400 --> 00:27:23,180
So what on earth did O-Con do?

464
00:27:24,744 --> 00:27:26,672
To be continued.

465
00:27:26,672 --> 00:27:29,967
How do you think they got that money?

466
00:27:32,136 --> 00:27:35,200
O-Con paid for it out of pocket, right?

467
00:27:35,200 --> 00:27:36,733
Your complexion...

468
00:27:36,733 --> 00:27:38,232
What's the matter?

469
00:27:38,232 --> 00:27:39,967
I'm just Kusakabe, a sole proprietor,

470
00:27:39,967 --> 00:27:42,312
paying for that on my own
as a necessary business expense.

471
00:27:42,312 --> 00:27:46,020
I mean, a consultant
paying out of pocket for our project,

472
00:27:46,020 --> 00:27:49,164
then having no money left to eat
and ending up malnourished.

473
00:27:49,164 --> 00:27:51,680
That's not okay! It's absolutely not okay!

474
00:27:51,680 --> 00:27:53,508
What are you talking about?

475
00:27:54,252 --> 00:27:57,196
It's for this character.
Everything we do is for it.

476
00:27:57,196 --> 00:28:00,700
That's not for its sake!

477
00:28:01,404 --> 00:28:03,180
Huh?

478
00:28:05,352 --> 00:28:07,104
What's this?

479
00:28:07,104 --> 00:28:08,688
Ah, no...

480
00:28:08,688 --> 00:28:10,572
This is...

481
00:28:10,572 --> 00:28:13,220
Takai Create! That one, right?

482
00:28:14,164 --> 00:28:15,616
Why were you hiding it?

483
00:28:15,616 --> 00:28:17,108
I wasn't hiding it.

484
00:28:17,108 --> 00:28:19,208
- I was going to tell you later.
- Is it about money?

485
00:28:19,208 --> 00:28:22,192
Blinded by money, you took that gig
with a shady company like that?

486
00:28:22,192 --> 00:28:24,208
If you get involved in something weird again,

487
00:28:24,208 --> 00:28:25,992
and this character
can't make its plushie debut,

488
00:28:25,992 --> 00:28:27,820
- that would be...
- That's why!

489
00:28:27,820 --> 00:28:30,832
You're the one who's getting involved
in something weird!

490
00:28:30,832 --> 00:28:32,224
You don't have enough food to eat, right?

491
00:28:32,224 --> 00:28:33,728
If you collapse
and our company goes bankrupt,

492
00:28:33,728 --> 00:28:35,968
our character won't be able to
make its plushie debut then, either!

493
00:28:35,968 --> 00:28:38,433
How is any of that for the character's sake?

494
00:28:44,672 --> 00:28:49,000
Working with that look on your face
just makes me more uneasy.

495
00:28:51,667 --> 00:28:53,760
I'm very sorry...

496
00:28:54,933 --> 00:28:56,833
for mixing personal and business matters.

497
00:28:59,884 --> 00:29:03,867
Please let me take some time off.

498
00:29:19,700 --> 00:29:23,768
To make it feel rounder here
and bring out a sense of childishness...

499
00:29:23,768 --> 00:29:26,400
The number of dots... Hey, are you listening?

500
00:29:27,124 --> 00:29:29,144
What time is it now?

501
00:29:29,144 --> 00:29:30,664
It's just before 7 o'clock. Why?

502
00:29:30,664 --> 00:29:33,080
Well, he said he'd transfer the fee today.

503
00:29:35,767 --> 00:29:40,668
<i>The number you have dialed
is in an area without signal...</i>

504
00:29:40,668 --> 00:29:42,272
What's the name of that other company?

505
00:29:42,272 --> 00:29:43,552
Takai Create.

506
00:29:43,552 --> 00:29:45,267
Takai Create?

507
00:29:45,267 --> 00:29:48,144
Huh? I feel like I've heard of
them before. Takai Create.

508
00:29:48,144 --> 00:29:49,919
Takai...

509
00:29:50,640 --> 00:29:52,232
Wait, look at this! Takai Create!

510
00:29:52,232 --> 00:29:53,376
[Fake Company Owner Busted in
Character Investment Fraud]

511
00:29:53,376 --> 00:29:55,233
Arrested on suspicion of
character investment fraud.

512
00:29:55,233 --> 00:29:56,460
Arrested?

513
00:29:56,460 --> 00:29:58,220
Wait, wait! Then what about the fee?

514
00:29:58,220 --> 00:30:01,300
Never mind that. First, contact Ms. Kusakabe.

515
00:30:05,264 --> 00:30:08,264
Well, calling her now on the phone is...

516
00:30:08,264 --> 00:30:09,396
Huh?

517
00:30:09,396 --> 00:30:11,664
What is it? Are you two fighting?

518
00:30:13,300 --> 00:30:16,248
You have to treasure Ms. Kusakabe, okay?

519
00:30:17,056 --> 00:30:18,816
There's no one else like her.

520
00:30:18,816 --> 00:30:23,044
Someone who understands both you
and this character that much.

521
00:30:23,044 --> 00:30:24,992
It's a miracle.

522
00:30:32,640 --> 00:30:38,524
[Mugi]

523
00:30:48,067 --> 00:30:49,860
Mr. Takai?

524
00:30:55,360 --> 00:30:56,532
[Fake Company Owner Busted in
Character Investment Fraud]

525
00:30:56,532 --> 00:30:58,458
Fraud?

526
00:31:00,100 --> 00:31:02,700
[Related Locations Also Searched]

527
00:31:14,164 --> 00:31:18,276
Well, I was originally alone anyway.

528
00:31:24,016 --> 00:31:25,836
Wow!

529
00:31:27,880 --> 00:31:30,020
I never thought you'd quit and go on a trip.

530
00:31:30,020 --> 00:31:32,416
Mr. Seo, there's something
I want to ask you...

531
00:31:32,416 --> 00:31:34,116
I know.

532
00:31:34,116 --> 00:31:35,780
I know, I do.

533
00:31:35,780 --> 00:31:38,600
- You know?
- I'll talk first.

534
00:31:39,208 --> 00:31:41,100
I'll talk about this properly.

535
00:31:50,552 --> 00:31:53,052
How should I say this?

536
00:31:53,052 --> 00:31:57,536
From a casual part-time job
to becoming a consultant,

537
00:31:57,536 --> 00:32:04,252
and as a result, a new character was created.

538
00:32:05,796 --> 00:32:10,567
But... you're always talking back,

539
00:32:10,567 --> 00:32:13,412
and always getting angry.

540
00:32:15,588 --> 00:32:17,974
What's with this mouth-sultant?

541
00:32:17,974 --> 00:32:20,648
Well, if this is going to be a long story,
then maybe later...

542
00:32:20,648 --> 00:32:22,240
But...

543
00:32:22,240 --> 00:32:29,476
even if just a tiny bit,

544
00:32:31,428 --> 00:32:33,572
it was fun, I thought.

545
00:32:37,972 --> 00:32:40,596
So, for everything up to now...

546
00:32:43,760 --> 00:32:44,944
thank you.

547
00:32:44,944 --> 00:32:48,100
What meaningless time spent!

548
00:32:48,784 --> 00:32:50,344
Huh?

549
00:32:50,344 --> 00:32:52,812
- I'll say it again.
- That's enough. Never again.

550
00:32:52,812 --> 00:32:53,844
More importantly, Mr. Seo,

551
00:32:53,844 --> 00:32:58,008
regarding the rights to the characters
you drew in your work with Takai Create,

552
00:32:58,008 --> 00:33:01,484
did you ever sign a contract
or make a verbal agreement?

553
00:33:01,484 --> 00:33:03,500
Wait, wait, wait, what about the characters?

554
00:33:03,500 --> 00:33:06,456
Did you say you'd give or transfer
the rights to Mr. Takai?

555
00:33:06,456 --> 00:33:08,524
Huh? I don't think I did.

556
00:33:08,524 --> 00:33:11,328
Really? This is important.
Are you absolutely sure?

557
00:33:11,328 --> 00:33:14,000
I didn't say I'd do that,
and he never asked about it either.

558
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:16,108
Understood. Do you have your passport?

559
00:33:16,108 --> 00:33:18,452
- Huh?
- Just bring it and come with me now.

560
00:33:18,452 --> 00:33:20,776
Huh? Where are we going?

561
00:33:20,776 --> 00:33:23,360
To the Republic of Textorian.

562
00:33:23,360 --> 00:33:26,344
- Tex...
- Mr. Takai was doing IP business there.

563
00:33:26,344 --> 00:33:29,260
Using the characters you drew
without permission.

564
00:33:29,260 --> 00:33:31,868
This character's local name is
Cho-cho-cho-cho-cho-cho-cho.

565
00:33:31,868 --> 00:33:33,868
Apparently, it's very popular with children.

566
00:33:33,868 --> 00:33:35,128
Cho-cho-cho-cho...

567
00:33:35,128 --> 00:33:39,567
Probably after tasting this success,
Mr. Takai had you draw new characters

568
00:33:39,567 --> 00:33:43,084
and was planning to expand profits further,
but he was arrested before he could.

569
00:33:43,084 --> 00:33:46,468
If you haven't transferred
the rights to Mr. Takai,

570
00:33:46,468 --> 00:33:50,356
then this Cho-cho-cho-cho-cho-cho-cho
belongs to you, the designer.

571
00:33:50,356 --> 00:33:52,136
We don't really have to go
all the way there, do we?

572
00:33:52,136 --> 00:33:54,128
No, we absolutely must go.

573
00:33:54,128 --> 00:33:56,027
Because... Because...

574
00:34:00,108 --> 00:34:01,732
It...

575
00:34:01,732 --> 00:34:05,512
Its design was stolen due to
someone's sloppy management.

576
00:34:05,512 --> 00:34:09,367
If this continues, it could also be misused!

577
00:34:10,592 --> 00:34:11,640
I see.

578
00:34:11,640 --> 00:34:14,752
Regarding this matter,
I also have some responsibility.

579
00:34:14,752 --> 00:34:16,952
Before saying "Oh, my" and "Get dumped",

580
00:34:16,952 --> 00:34:20,388
I should have properly
handled these procedures.

581
00:34:20,388 --> 00:34:24,012
IP business often draws attention to
the profit aspect, but it's not just that.

582
00:34:24,012 --> 00:34:26,592
It's also about the right
to protect these characters.

583
00:34:26,592 --> 00:34:30,004
So, this fight, we will definitely win it.

584
00:34:30,944 --> 00:34:34,452
For its sake as well,
we'll absolutely win it!

585
00:34:34,452 --> 00:34:36,212
Yeah.

586
00:34:39,280 --> 00:34:40,588
[Mr. Mizuki Seo]

587
00:34:40,588 --> 00:34:42,856
So it was making this much money?
Cho-cho-cho-cho...

588
00:34:42,856 --> 00:34:45,600
Like I said, Ms. Kusakabe
is amazing. She really is.

589
00:34:45,600 --> 00:34:47,696
In a country where the language is different,

590
00:34:47,696 --> 00:34:52,784
she won the rights for Cho-cho-cho-cho,
and protected its rights too.

591
00:34:53,692 --> 00:34:58,716
Do you understand? From now on,
royalties will be coming in.

592
00:34:58,716 --> 00:35:01,808
Really amazing. Incredibly amazing.

593
00:35:01,808 --> 00:35:04,964
Well, I was there too, on the ground.

594
00:35:04,964 --> 00:35:07,267
You were just signing, right?
On the contract.

595
00:35:07,267 --> 00:35:12,588
No, no, no. I also ran the bath
and did the cleaning.

596
00:35:12,588 --> 00:35:18,084
There's a concept in IP that human talent
is also intellectual property,

597
00:35:18,084 --> 00:35:22,567
and I think you need to
properly grasp that too.

598
00:35:24,904 --> 00:35:28,520
Anyway, I didn't come here
to talk about that.

599
00:35:28,520 --> 00:35:30,696
I'm here because it's arriving soon.

600
00:35:37,967 --> 00:35:39,792
Thanks for your hard work.

601
00:36:44,232 --> 00:36:46,924
Zapaan.

602
00:36:50,292 --> 00:36:52,168
Good morning.

603
00:37:03,408 --> 00:37:05,380
So,

604
00:37:05,380 --> 00:37:09,176
regarding the Cute Think Tank,
I need a quick word.

605
00:37:10,132 --> 00:37:12,240
Yes?

606
00:37:12,240 --> 00:37:16,948
I'd like you to disband it for now.

607
00:37:16,948 --> 00:37:18,836
May I ask why?

608
00:37:18,836 --> 00:37:22,848
Because you're paying those people
out of your own pocket,

609
00:37:22,848 --> 00:37:24,708
a considerable amount.

610
00:37:25,348 --> 00:37:27,708
And I... can't enjoy that.

611
00:37:27,708 --> 00:37:33,680
If making the plushie is built on
someone else's burden, I can't enjoy it.

612
00:37:35,908 --> 00:37:38,436
I want you to eat properly.

613
00:37:39,176 --> 00:37:43,076
Even though it's annoying, like usual,

614
00:37:43,692 --> 00:37:45,984
it's better if you get angry at me.

615
00:37:45,984 --> 00:37:49,632
How should I say this... It feels right.

616
00:37:49,632 --> 00:37:51,524
It's really annoying, though.

617
00:37:55,212 --> 00:37:59,033
It's not just for the character. It's for me.

618
00:38:00,464 --> 00:38:06,064
But for me becomes for us,

619
00:38:06,728 --> 00:38:13,404
and for us becomes
for the character, I think.

620
00:38:16,540 --> 00:38:20,567
I see. Understood.

621
00:38:22,844 --> 00:38:24,667
I'm sorry.

622
00:38:25,400 --> 00:38:29,340
For always causing a commotion.

623
00:38:29,340 --> 00:38:30,340
Alright.

624
00:38:35,960 --> 00:38:40,367
Well then, this is urgent.
The documents and data entry.

625
00:38:42,864 --> 00:38:44,740
Okay.

626
00:38:56,780 --> 00:39:00,064
[Its Backstory Proposal]

627
00:39:00,064 --> 00:39:02,008
Well...

628
00:39:14,388 --> 00:39:18,744
[Its Backstory Proposal]

629
00:39:26,100 --> 00:39:33,484
It is a hyena boy who was
born on a planet called Planet Tutu.

630
00:39:33,484 --> 00:39:38,148
He lives in a burrow
and is always alone for some reason.

631
00:39:38,896 --> 00:39:42,633
Maybe everyone is scared
because he is a hyena.

632
00:39:43,572 --> 00:39:48,033
He wants friends,
but he can't muster the courage.

633
00:39:50,616 --> 00:39:57,436
Then, one day, he really wanted to
see a dance called ballet on Earth,

634
00:39:58,824 --> 00:40:05,280
because everyone was wearing a fluffy thing
just like the one on his belly.

635
00:40:09,168 --> 00:40:13,880
He gathered his courage,
jumped out of his burrow, and went to Earth,

636
00:40:14,692 --> 00:40:19,012
but he still felt lonely and was downcast.

637
00:40:20,928 --> 00:40:25,884
A person on Earth who saw him said,

638
00:40:27,580 --> 00:40:33,167
"That fluffy thing is cute,
like a ballet tutu."

639
00:40:46,172 --> 00:40:51,433
He cheered up and came to
love the fluffy thing even more.

640
00:40:53,620 --> 00:40:58,267
"I hope I can cheer everyone up too."

641
00:42:04,276 --> 00:42:06,104
I'm sorry for becoming like this
all of a sudden.

642
00:42:06,104 --> 00:42:08,892
I know it's an important time.

643
00:42:10,728 --> 00:42:12,728
This is really selfish of me, but...

644
00:42:16,728 --> 00:42:19,332
I got dumped.

645
00:42:19,332 --> 00:42:21,892
But that's not work-related, right?

646
00:42:21,892 --> 00:42:23,656
But...

647
00:42:24,264 --> 00:42:26,496
it just feels weird.

648
00:42:28,640 --> 00:42:31,268
I'm sorry.

649
00:42:31,268 --> 00:42:34,836
Really, talking about this... Really.

650
00:42:46,456 --> 00:42:48,612
It just arrived.

651
00:42:51,556 --> 00:42:55,733
Its name is Tutu-Tuesla.

652
00:43:01,388 --> 00:43:07,228
Tutu is from the memory
you told me about the other day,

653
00:43:07,228 --> 00:43:09,700
from Jigoku-guruma Ballerina.

654
00:43:10,344 --> 00:43:18,344
And Tuesla apparently means
"You are there" in French.

655
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:49,640
Mr. Seo.

656
00:43:51,436 --> 00:43:56,624
I'm being supported right now...

657
00:43:59,112 --> 00:44:00,860
by it.

658
00:44:11,580 --> 00:44:14,167
Thank you, Mr. Seo.

659
00:44:26,536 --> 00:44:30,567
Welcome, Tutu-Tuesla.

660
00:44:35,552 --> 00:44:37,424
Cute.

661
00:44:45,316 --> 00:44:47,176
Cute...
